From c220b32f5d1f1ea84405ded89ad9a1588421e16c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:04:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/76] rc3-instr 5/8: bound the QSA indexer page-table values
 (Luna guard 1)

Both indexer logits kernels read a page id out of the page table and use it as
an address with no bound:

    physical_page = tl.load(page_table_ptr + request * stride_table_req
                            + logical_page, mask=live, other=0)
    keys = tl.load(k_cache_ptr + physical_page[:, None].to(tl.int64)
                   * stride_cache_block + ...)

The mask bounds WHICH ENTRY is read, never the VALUE that comes back. A stale
or freed page id therefore becomes k_cache_ptr + page * stride_cache_block and
the SM faults. This is the S2 illegal-address shape.

The QSA attention kernel in the same model already does the right thing
(nvidia/qsa.py:137): it ANDs the page bound into its live mask and clamps the
page before the multiply. The AMD mirror does the same (amd/ops/qsa.py:86-88).
This commit brings the two indexer kernels in line with their own tree.

Shape of the recording (review E7): the guard sits inside a pipelined
`tl.range(num_stages=STAGES)` loop, so the reduction and the atomic are NOT in
the loop body. Each iteration accumulates a per-lane int32 count and a per-lane
worst column in registers; after the loop there is one tl.sum, one tl.max and,
only if the count is non-zero, three atomics. A clean program executes no
atomic at all.

Launch-site audit for this signature (review B2, which caught exactly this
omission in round 1):
  * _qsa_mqa_paged_prefill_kernel -- one launch, qsa_indexer.py:404
    (_prefill_logits). No warmup registration.
  * _qsa_mqa_paged_uniform_kernel -- one launch, qsa_indexer.py:535
    (qsa_select_paged_decode), AND the JIT warmup at qsa_indexer.py:348
    (warmup_qsa_mqa_paged_decode), which passes eleven positionals and is
    updated here with k_cache.shape[0] and a TritonWarmupTensor(torch.int64)
    counter. Missing this in round 1 would have broken startup warmup.
  * No AMD mirror: vllm/models/qwen4_exp/amd/ops/ has only hc.py and qsa.py,
    and neither contains an indexer logits kernel.

ROUND 3: _GUARD_BIAS is bound as tl.constexpr. Round 2 declared it as a plain
module-level int, which a @triton.jit body cannot read, and the GPU smoke
failed every guarded-kernel test with "NameError: Cannot access global variable
_GUARD_BIAS". Checked the other module-level names in this file: none are
referenced from a jit body.

Draft for Astra review. Not merged into any RC.
---
 .../qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa_indexer.py       | 76 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 72 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa_indexer.py b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa_indexer.py
index 7efcc9077..9b7cef424 100644
--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa_indexer.py
